From 41d6ffea35375be4923a9fa021da9c54024d63a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude review <review@example.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:56:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] TPF and derived-quantity ranges; shared toroidal profile;
 error-model cleanup

Review issue 5 and Phase 6 (the uncertainty patch, ported to the current
code), S1, S2, S6, and the camera-location lookup.

Toroidal profile and TPF (issue 5)
- _post_process_calculations uses uncertainty.toroidal_profile, the same
  function as the ranges: evaluated at the fitted peak location itself (no
  snapping to the grid), no sample deleted, mean over the periodic grid
- radDist total power: mean x 2 pi over the uniform periodic grid; the
  Simpson rule missed the interval from the last sample back to 2 pi
- _bestFit_radDist_parameters/_scaling, now unused, are removed

Ranges (new emis3d/uncertainty.py)
- Median and 68%/95% ranges for TPF, total power, peak location, peak power,
  power fraction near the peak, amplitude and decay lengths, combining
  parameter covariance, near-equivalent radDists (Akaike weights from the
  same AIC that ranks the fits) and optional per-camera calibration draws
- Samples recompute derived parameters, so a fitted peak location
  (peak_rad_loc from peak_shift) gets a real range
- Refits use the shared Util_emis3D.fit_radDist
- Emis3D._post_process_uncertainty stores bestFits[t]["ranges"]; called by
  _perform_fits and scripts/run_emis3D.py before _cleanup_fits
- RunConfig gains an `uncertainty:` block (validated; calibration only for
  configured cameras); on by default, `enabled: false` turns it off
- `emis3d calibrate` also prints an `uncertainty: calibration:` block from
  each camera's measured spread

Plots
- TPF panel: profile with 68%/95% bands and the TPF range in the title; the
  peak marker spans the axis (S1: axvline's ymin/ymax were given data values)
- Saved figures are closed (S2)

Error models (S6)
- signal_error raises on an unknown name instead of returning None
- "inverse" removed: the same shape as "constant", and the overall error
  scale changes neither the fit nor its ranking
- "inverse square" renamed "poisson" (fractional error ~ 1/sqrt(signal));
  RunConfig explains both changes

Camera locations
- _post_process_bolo_locations compared camera names with channel names and
  never matched, so the step scale's locations were always empty; cameras
  are now matched by their channels

Tests: tests/test_uncertainty.py (14, including interval coverage over 120
noisy datasets) and tests/test_results.py (5) through Emis3D on fabricated
MOCK data; error-model tests updated.
